<title>USA: Bayer, Roche in joint pact - NYT.</title>
<headline>Bayer, Roche in joint pact - NYT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bayer AG and Roche Holding Ltd are starting a joint venture in the United States to sell Roche's Aleve analgesic and other products, the New York Times reported Monday.</p>
<p>Roche took over the Aleve line, which had sales of $200 million last year, from Procter &amp; Gamble Co in June.</p>
<p>The combined sales of all the products covered in the marketing venture totaled about $800 million last year, the Times reported.</p>
<p>--New York Newsdesk  (212) 859-1610</p>
